The review diff viewer uses unmodified npm packages @pierre/diffs 1.6.2,
@pierre/highlights 0.3.0, @pierre/theme 2.0.0 and @pierre/theming 1.0.2.
These packages are licensed under Apache-2.0; their identical license text is
preserved in licenses/pierre-Apache-2.0.txt. Upstream bundled theme attributions
are retained verbatim in licenses/pierre-highlights-NOTICE.md and
licenses/pierre-theme-NOTICE.md. Package versions and integrity are pinned in
package-lock.json. Diff presentation and syntax theme settings were reconstructed
from the user-supplied local Codex desktop reference; original compiled app
modules are excluded from source and release archives. The reference bundle's
exact Pierre package version has not been established.

AnyWork desktop can bundle cloudflared (Cloudflare, Apache-2.0) and tunwg
(Nitin Jain and contributors, MIT). Android uses the official WireGuard tunnel
library 1.0.20260102 (WireGuard LLC, Apache-2.0; embedded wireguard-go components
retain their MIT notices). See licenses/ and docs/desktop-manager.md.

The Rust/Tauri desktop manager bundles Noto Sans SC Regular from the official
Noto CJK subset distribution. Copyright and SIL Open Font License 1.1 are
preserved in licenses/NotoSansSC-OFL.txt.

Subagent avatar SVG resources in the public distribution are original geometric
illustrations generated for AnyWork, with deterministic light/dark variants.
The proprietary desktop application's extracted avatars and compiled modules
are not included in this distribution or its public Git history.
